   $q$Read the sentence: "There are many students who walk to school when the weather is nice." Which revision is the most concise?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Many students walk to school in nice weather.","is_correct":true},{"text":"There are many students walking to school in nice weather.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"keeps-wordiness"},{"text":"Students walk.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"drops-key-meaning"},{"text":"Many of the students who walk to school do so when it is nice.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"keeps-wordiness"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Many students walk to school in nice weather.$q$, $q$Dropping "There are ... who" makes "students" the subject and "walk" the verb, so the sentence is shorter and direct. "Students walk" cuts so much that the meaning is lost.$q$, 'draft', null)
