   $q$In a letter to the principal, a student writes, "It is believed by many students that the lunch period should be extended." Which revision is most direct and persuasive?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The lunch period should be extended, it is believed by many.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"still-passive"},{"text":"It is thought by students that lunch could maybe be longer.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"hedging-weakens-claim"},{"text":"Many students believe the lunch period should be longer.","is_correct":true},{"text":"A longer lunch period is believed to be wanted by many students.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"still-passive"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Many students believe the lunch period should be longer.$q$, $q$The active voice makes "many students" the subject, so the reader sees who holds the opinion and the claim sounds confident. The other choices keep a passive verb, and one adds hedging that weakens the request.$q$, 'draft', null)
